  "headline": "India's Garden City and Tech Capital",
  "short_description": "Bengaluru pairs a temperate climate and green parks with its status as India's leading technology hub.",
  "about": "Once known as the Garden City for its parks and lakes, Bengaluru (Bangalore) is now India's technology and startup capital, while retaining royal Wadiyar-era heritage nearby.\n\nLocated on the Deccan Plateau in southern Karnataka at around 900 m elevation, giving it a mild climate.\n\nA cosmopolitan mix of Kannadiga heritage and a large migrant tech workforce; known for its pub and cafe culture.\n\nPredominantly Hindu with significant Muslim and Christian communities.",
  "history": "Founded by Kempe Gowda I in the 16th century; grew rapidly through cantonment-era development and post-independence as India's electronics and IT hub.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Kempegowda International Airport (airport)\n- Krantivira Sangolli Rayanna Railway Station (railway)\n- Kempegowda Bus Station (Majestic) (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Kannada, English, Hindi\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to February",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2 days",
  "nearest_airport": "Kempegowda International Airport (BLR)",
  "nearest_railway_station": "Krantivira Sangolli Rayanna (Bengaluru City) Railway Station",
